  <rules>
    <rule name="Subterranean" id="ee55-da2d-3a6a-4bd3" hidden="false">
      <description>Commonwealth Forces can field Subterranean units.


In the Deployment Step, all units with the Subterranean trait must be placed in Reserve. When a unit is placed in Reserve in this manner, their General must place a
Subterranean Marker anywhere in their Deployment Zone.


If, at the start of the Clash, either General has any units in Reserve with the Subterranean trait, then do not skip the Deploy Reserves step of the first round Ready Phase.


At the start of the Deploy Reserves Step of each Round, the General can choose to move any of these markers up to 10”, in a straight line, ignoring all Terrain and enemy
units.


A Subterranean Marker cannot end this move within the Footprint of another model, Terrain Feature or marker.


Any units that a Subterranean Marker moves through must take a Suppression Test at the end of this move. Aircraft, Rotorcraft, and units with the Large special rule are unaffected. Similarly, all units can move across Subterranean Markers. An Aerial unit cannot end its move within the Footprint of a Subterranean Marker.


If any other unit ends its move within the Footprint of a Subterranean Marker, then the opposing General must move it the minimum distance to ensure it is no longer
being overlapped. 
If a unit moves through or onto a Subterranean Marker, the unit must take a Suppression Test at the end of its move. Aircraft, Rotorcraft, and units with the Large special rule do not have to take this Suppression Test.


If a Subterranean Marker moves through a Defensible Building, its General must roll an Attack Die at the end of its move. If the die scores a Heroic Strike, place a Wrecked status token on the building - it can no longer be Garrisoned by units that do not have the Occupy special rule, and is treated as Blocking Terrain for the rest of the game.


If there is a unit Garrisoning the building, it must make an immediate Exit manoeuvre (as described on page 43 of the Armoured Clash Rulebook).


Instead of Activating a unit on the Battlefield, a General may choose to Activate a Subterranean unit in Reserve. This unit is immediately deployed onto the Battlefield so
that it is within 3” of one of the General’s Subterranean Markers, with no models within 1” of any enemy units, Defensible Buildings or Strategic Objective Markers.


If a Subterranean unit is activated during the First Round, then it must be deployed wholly within its General’s Deployment Zone. Note that Subterranean Markers
are not tied to any particular unit, so any Subterranean unit that is still in Reserve can enter the Battlefield from any Subterranean Marker.


The Subterranean Marker is immediately removed from the battlefield and the unit Activates as normal.


Subterranean units cannot be deployed in the final round of a Clash. Any Subterranean units that are still in Reserve at this point will take no part in the battle.</description>
    </rule>
  </rules>
